// 5:3, three equal bars of 1. The image is 330 pixels high, so a unit is 110 pixels. The equals sign's
// bars are 113 by 32 pixels, 1.027 by 0.291, centered 278.5 across, 2.573, and 138.5 and 182.5 down.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Egalitarian Polyamory Pride Flag"
  designer "NonMonoPrideFlags (DeviantArt)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2015-12-30"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20220208163038/https://www.deviantart.com/nonmonoprideflags/art/Egalitarian-Polyamory-Pride-Flag-581140334"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20120213104012/http://www.isomedia.com/homes/jene/flag.html"
  note "NonMonoPrideFlags's DeviantArt post 'Egalitarian Polyamory Pride Flag', as the Wayback Machine held it on 8 February 2022, says: 'This is my pride flag design for Egalitarian Polyamory, which can also be called Democratic Polyamory', in which all partners are considered equal, and: 'The design is based off of the polyamory flag, with all the colors tinted purple (the color for equality) and with the yellow pi symbol replaced by an equal sign.' The post is dated 30 December 2015 (UTC)."
  note "What is taken from Jim Evans's polyamory flag (polyamory-pi in this collection) is its layout, three equal bars with a yellow symbol in the middle, and its colors' order. The pi glyph isn't used. The colors are the designer's own purple-tinted ones, not Evans's."
  note "The post's image, the original file, is a JPEG of 541 by 330 pixels, 1.64:1, as are all this designer's flags of that month, so no deliberate proportion is clear. This file uses the common 5:3 rather than the polyamory flag's 3:2. The image draws three equal bars, of 108 or 109 pixels each."
  note "The colors are read from the image's pixels, which are flat: violet #460ab8, magenta #d60d8f, black #000000 and yellow #fef200."
  note "The equals sign is built from two rectangles, an approximation of the designer's drawing, with the sizes and places the image gives them. Its bars measure 31 and 33 pixels high, and are both 32 here. The sign sits about 8 pixels toward the fly of the center and 4 above it, as in the image."
}
palette {
  violet "#460ab8"
  magenta "#d60d8f"
  black "#000000"
  yellow "#fef200"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars violet magenta black

charge rect yellow {
  at fly=2.573 hoist=1.259
  at fly=2.573 hoist=1.659
  fly 1.027
  hoist 0.291
}
